# Patterns lychee should skip when checking links.
# One regex per line. See: https://lychee.cli.rs/usage/excludes/

# Local-development URLs that only resolve on a running booth.
^https?://localhost(:\d+)?(/|$)

# LinkedIn returns 403 to non-browser user agents — known false positive.
^https?://(www\.)?linkedin\.com/

# The CodingBooth blog lives at codingbooth.io/blog/ and is a separate static site
# built from blog/ and deployed at publish time — it doesn't exist in this
# repo, so the nav link to it can't be resolved here. Matches the root-relative nav
# href (and per-post links like /blog/welcome/title.html) and any absolute form; other
# codingbooth.io / nawaman.net/blog links stay checked.
^/blog(/|$)
codingbooth\.io/blog(/|$)
